    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19">

                <pb facs="0324" n="10" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg10"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.0012/538</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgenthau</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-07T16:00:00+02:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">October 7, 1914, 4 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9:30 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>My telegram of September 7.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d19-f1"/> Your telegram October
                    5, 2 p.m. Contents thereof concerning arbitration communicated to the Foreign
                    Office. Latter says on account of extra work due to the question of
                    capitulations they have been unable to give it desired attention but will do so
                    now.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
